      "id": "ermeniyye-i-sugra",
      "end": 1599,
      "contributors": [],
      "provenance": "Pleiades",
      "associationCertaintyURI": "https://pleiades.stoa.org/vocabularies/association-certainty/certain",
      "start": 1500,
      "details": "<p><em>FA\u1e62L MEMLEKET-\u0130 EFRENC VE ERMEN VE NA\u1e62\u0100R\u0100 BEY\u0100NI\u00a0VE \u1e2aULEF\u0100-YI MES\u012a\u1e24 \u0130\u2018L\u0100NI \u1e94\u0130KR\u0130NDED\u00dcR\u00a0</em><span>(Section: Description of the Lands of the Franks, Armenians, and Christians, and Mention of the Successors of the Messiah):\u00a0Let it not remain hidden that the\u00a0</span><em>\u1e25ud\u016bd-\u0131 vil\u0101yet-i Ermen</em><span>\u00a0(boundaries of the Armenian province) form a vast land opposite\u00a0</span><em>G\u00fcrcist\u0101n</em><span>\u00a0(Georgia).Its capital districts are\u00a0</span><em>Ermeniyye-i \u1e62u\u0121r\u0101</em><span>\u00a0(Armenia Minor) and\u00a0</span><em>Ermeniyye-i K\u00fcbr\u0101</em><span>\u00a0(Greater Armenia).The length (\u1e6d\u016bl) of\u00a0</span><em>Ermeniyye-i K\u00fcbr\u0101</em><span>\u00a0stretches from the frontier of\u00a0</span><em>\u0100zerbayc\u0101n</em><span>\u00a0(Azerbaijan) to the boundary of\u00a0</span><em>Selm\u0101s</em><span>\u00a0(Salmas, Iran).Its breadth (\u2018ar\u017c) extends from the beginning of the\u00a0</span><em>G\u00fcrcist\u0101n</em><span>\u00a0(Georgia) province to the farthest limit of\u00a0</span><em>Ves\u1e6d\u0101n</em><span>. As for\u00a0</span><em>Ermeniyye-i \u1e62u\u0121r\u0101</em><span>\u00a0(Armenia Minor), its length reaches from the Syrian side (</span><em>\u015e\u0101m \u1e6daraf\u0131</em><span>) to the extreme frontier of the\u00a0</span><em>vil\u0101yet-i R\u016bm</em><span>\u00a0(Anatolia). Likewise, its breadth runs from the frontier of\u00a0</span><em>Mal\u0101\u1e6diyye</em><span>\u00a0(Malatya) to the border of\u00a0</span><em>An\u1e6d\u0101kiyye</em><span>\u00a0(Antioch). All directions, regions, and mountains are included within this territory. In ancient times, there were five inhabited principal towns, which were called:\u00a0</span><em>Ay\u0101s</em><span>\u00a0(Yumurtal\u0131k, Turkey),\u00a0</span><em>S\u012bs</em><span>\u00a0(Kozan, Turkey),\u00a0</span><em>\u1e6cars\u016bs</em><span>\u00a0(Tarsus, Turkey),\u00a0</span><em>Adana</em><span>\u00a0(Adana, Turkey), and\u00a0</span><em>Mis\u012bs</em><span>\u00a0(Misis / Yakap\u0131nar, Turkey). All of them lie near one another. In our time, the largest of these towns is\u00a0</span><em>Adana</em><span>.\u00a0</span><em>Mis\u012bs</em><span>\u00a0and\u00a0</span><em>Ay\u0101s</em><span>\u00a0are in ruins, while\u00a0</span><em>S\u012bs</em><span>\u00a0and\u00a0</span><em>\u1e6cars\u016bs</em><span>\u00a0have become towns of medium size. In former days, the region had twenty thousand inhabited villages and fertile settlements; it is reported that today no tithe (</span><em>\u2018\u00f6\u015fr</em><span>) remains from them. Among its products:\u00a0</span><em>\u1e63\u016bf</em><span>\u00a0(woollen cloth), called\u00a0</span><em>\u1e33uds\u012b</em><span>, is said to be woven in\u00a0</span><em>An\u1e33ara</em><span>\u00a0(Ankara), which is subject to the\u00a0</span><em>vil\u0101yet-i R\u016bm</em><span>. And\u00a0</span><em>l\u0101den</em><span>\u00a0(labdanum; fragrant resin), renowned for its delightful scent, is produced on the nearby\u00a0</span><em>Cez\u012bre-i \u1e32\u0131br\u0131s</em><span>\u00a0(the Island of Cyprus). [translation]</span></p>",
